{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction for criminal offenses against the landlord (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1(o)-(r))","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant convicted of, or found liable for, assault, threats, theft on the premises, drug activity or human trafficking against the landlord, family or employees after a three-day Notice to Quit; suit must be filed within two years.","key_value":"3-day Notice to Quit; 2-year limit","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; also a tenant who knowingly permits such a person to reside on the premises continuously or occasionally.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"All residential rental tenancies in New Jersey"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No eviction suit may be brought more than two years after: the juvenile was found to be delinquent; conviction of the person; or after the person’s release from incarceration, whichever is later.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction from owner-occupied two- and three-family dwellings (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2(a))","requirement":"A tenant of a landlord-occupied two- or three-family dwelling may be removed only by court order, for holding over, nonpayment of rent, disorderly conduct, damage, rule or lease violations or non-renewal, with a three-month, one-month or three-day notice to quit as specified.","key_value":"3-month, 1-month or 3-day notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings; a court order for eviction is required.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":3,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2","quoted_span":"A three-day written Notice to Quit is required for any of the causes described as disorderly, destructive or violative of written rules or lease provisions (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2(a)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rooming and boarding house eviction causes and notice","requirement":"Owners of rooming and boarding houses must follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, unless the Bureau orders otherwise, and must give the County Welfare Board at least three working days' notice before starting an eviction.","key_value":"3 working days' notice to County Welfare Board","coverage_conditions":"Rooming and boarding houses: buildings with at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms, unless a Rooming and Boarding House Act exception applies.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rooming and boarding houses"},"exemptions":"Hotels with more than 85 percent temporary occupancy by people with homes elsewhere, school and college dormitories, buildings housing only college students and certain residences for the disabled.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3","quoted_span":"require owners of rooming and boarding houses to follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, except if otherwise ordered by the Bureau (N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)). There is a further requirement that the owner give at least three (3) working days’ notice to the County Welfare Board before starting the eviction action for any resident","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Penalties for owner move-in and demolition evictions (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6)","requirement":"A landlord who evicts a tenant to personally occupy the unit must occupy it for at least six months; after an eviction to board up, demolish or retire a building from residential use, the property may not be used residentially for five years.","key_value":"6 months' owner occupancy; 5-year residential-use ban; up to $10,000 civil penalty","coverage_conditions":"Applies where a tenant vacates after an owner move-in notice or after notice that the building is to be permanently boarded up, demolished or retired from residential use.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Owner move-in and demolition evictions"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the damages suffered plus attorney fees and costs; a civil penalty up to $10,000.00 for each violation of the five-year restriction.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6","quoted_span":"When a tenant vacates a dwelling unit after having been given notice that the landlord wishes to personally occupy the unit the landlord must occupy the unit for at least six (6) months.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-reprisal protection for tenants (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10)","requirement":"A landlord may not evict, substantially alter the lease or refuse to renew in reprisal for a tenant enforcing lease or legal rights, making a good faith complaint to a government authority, organizing, or refusing lease changes made in reprisal.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"All residential rental properties, including mobile homes"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","penalty":"The tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Foreclosure eviction notice requirements (N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69 et seq.)","requirement":"Before a tenant may be evicted because of foreclosure, the buyer who wants to occupy the property as a primary residence must give a 90-day notice to quit, and any person acquiring a foreclosed property must notify tenants in English and Spanish within 10 business days after the sale.","key_value":"90-day notice to quit; 10 business days' notice after sale","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in foreclosed properties, including month-to-month tenancies and owner-occupied two- and three-family units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Foreclosed residential rental properties"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69","quoted_span":"Any person acquiring a foreclosed property containing one or more residential rental units must provide notices to the tenants in English and Spanish, within 10 business days after the sale, letting tenants know that ownership has changed hands and that the tenants are not required to move because of the foreclosure.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act","requirement":"Tenants who are at least 62, permanently disabled, or disabled veterans of certain service, and who lived in the building a year before the conversion was recorded, may be protected from eviction for 40 years if family income is within the limit.","key_value":"40 years' protection; income up to 3 times county average per person or $50,000.00, whichever is greater","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in buildings being converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership who meet the age, disability or veteran and one-year residency requirements.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Buildings converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county or $50,000.00, whichever is greater (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992 protected tenancy","requirement":"Qualified tenants in qualified counties in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible as senior citizens or disabled persons under the 1981 Act are protected; Hudson County is the only qualified county.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Qualified tenants in qualified counties, currently only Hudson County, in buildings converted or being converted.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Conversion tenants in Hudson County"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"The Tenant Protection Law of 1992 amendment extends protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible for Protected Tenancy as either Senior Citizens or Disabled Persons under the “Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act of 1981” (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40 to -61.59; N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.1 to -3.4).","interaction":"Extends protected tenancy to tenants not eligible under the 1981 Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
